  <section class="scene founder-note">
    <div class="narrow center-text science-head">
      <p class="kicker reveal">A note from our founder</p>
      <h2 class="reveal d1">I've always understood what a good night is worth.</h2>
      <p class="invest-lead reveal d1" style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.82)">Sleep was never a trend to me &mdash; it's something I've paid close attention to for as long as I can remember, long before it had a hashtag. I started Nottera because I wanted to turn that attention into something useful for other people, not just a better pillow.</p>
      <p class="invest-lead reveal d2" style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.82)">My goal is to make sleep science easy to actually use &mdash; a few honest minutes a day, not another feed to scroll through. That's why the Journal exists, and why it will keep growing alongside everything else we make.</p>
      <p class="invest-lead reveal d2" style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.82)">Nottera will keep evolving with what our customers actually need &mdash; new products, new research, new ways to sleep better &mdash; starting here in the U.S., where sleep quietly shapes next-day performance, mental health, creativity, and even long-term cardiovascular and immune health far more than most people realize.<sup>1</sup> The pillow was the beginning. Helping people sleep better, at scale, is the point.</p>
      <p class="reveal d2" style="margin-top:2rem;font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-weight:600;font-size:1.6rem;letter-spacing:.015em;color:#A8935F">&mdash; Founder &amp; CEO, Nottera</p>
      <p class="reveal d2" style="margin-top:1rem;font-size:.78rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.45)">Source: <sup>1</sup>CDC, Division of Sleep and Sleep Disorders &mdash; sleep insufficiency is linked to increased risk of heart disease, type 2 diabetes, obesity, and depression, alongside impaired next-day cognitive and emotional function.</p>
