  <!-- ============ SCENE 10 · FAQ ============ -->
  <section class="scene faq">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="kicker reveal">Before you decide</p>
      <h2 class="reveal d1">Quiet answers.</h2>
      <div class="accordion reveal d2" id="faq">
        <p class="faq-group">The Nottera Pillow</p>
        <details>
          <summary>Which sleeping positions does it support?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>All of them. The wave contour cradles side sleepers, supports back sleepers, and stays low and soft for stomach sleepers. It adapts to you — you don't have to adapt to it.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is it firm or soft?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>One universal feel: a medium-firm adaptive memory foam at roughly 48D density &mdash; dense enough to hold its shape night after night, soft enough to cradle your head and neck under warmth and weight, then spring back by morning.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Will it fit my body and height?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. Each size has two loft heights, so you can do the <strong>Phase Flip</strong> — turn the pillow over to change how it sits under your neck. Crescent runs 10cm on the high side and 7cm on the low side; Eclipse runs 12cm and 10cm. Broad-shouldered and side sleepers tend to prefer the higher side of whichever size they have; a flatter, closer feel comes from the lower side.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does it sleep hot?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>No. The open-cell memory foam and the knitted cover &mdash; a breathable 95% polyester / 5% spandex blend at 320g/m&sup2; &mdash; move air instead of trapping it, so it stays cooler than dense, traditional memory foam through the night.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How much does the pillow weigh?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Crescent (standard) weighs 0.55kg; Eclipse (oversized) weighs 0.9kg. That weight comes from real foam density, not filler &mdash; light enough to travel with, substantial enough to hold its shape.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How long does it take to adjust?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Most people feel the difference the first night. Give your body up to a week to fully settle into the new alignment.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I care for the pillow?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Simple. The knitted cover unzips and is machine washable cold &mdash; air-dry it and it comes back softer. Never machine-wash or soak the foam core; spot-clean it and let it air out, away from direct sun.</p></div>
        </details>

        <p class="faq-group">Pillowcases</p>
        <details>
          <summary>What is the pillowcase made of?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>A cooling <strong>ice-silk</strong> weave &mdash; smooth and silky against skin and hair, cool to the touch, and gentle enough for everyday use at a friendly price.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is it better for my skin and hair than cotton?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes &mdash; far kinder than cotton. Less friction means fewer creases, less frizz, and less moisture drawn from your skin overnight.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Will the pillowcase fit my pillow?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Each case is cut to fit the ergonomic contour of the Nottera Pillow. Choose the size that matches your pillow &mdash; Crescent (standard) or Eclipse (oversized) &mdash; and it slips on with a clean, hidden closure.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I care for the pillowcase?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Machine wash cold on a gentle cycle with like colours, then tumble low or line dry. No bleach. It stays smooth and cool wash after wash.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Why buy a pillowcase on its own?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Because the case is the part that touches your skin and hair every night &mdash; it's the piece worth upgrading, and the easiest way to refresh your bed. Buy one alone, collect a few colours, or add one to your pillow as a set.</p></div>
        </details>

        <p class="faq-group">Orders, shipping &amp; returns</p>
        <details>
          <summary>When will my order arrive?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Every order is prepared and quality-checked before it leaves us, then delivered within <strong>7&ndash;14 days</strong> &mdash; fully tracked, so you can follow it the whole way.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How does it arrive?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Compact, in quiet recyclable packaging. Take it out, let it breathe and fully expand for a few hours, and it's ready for its first night.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where do you ship, and is it free?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>We ship across the United States, fully tracked, in 7&ndash;14 days. Shipping is <strong>free on every pillow, no minimum</strong>. Pillowcases ship free on orders over $65.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I get the free Sleep Guide?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes &mdash; the digital Nottera Sleep Guide is included <strong>free with every order over $100</strong>, delivered to your inbox. Science-backed habits for deeper, faster sleep.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What if it isn't for me?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body"><p>You get <strong>60 nights</strong> to actually find out &mdash; not a five-minute test in a showroom. If it isn't right by then, return it for a full refund, no questions asked; returned pillows are donated, not resold. Pillowcases follow our standard 30-day policy for unopened items, for hygiene reasons. Anything that arrives damaged or faulty, we always make right.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

